# Everything build.py regenerates.  Its header says "Everything below is
# REGENERATED", and `python3 build.py --clean` deletes exactly this.  A clean
# rebuild reproduces every fab output byte for byte (the board file itself
# differs only in uuids that pcbnew rewrites as it pours the zones -- see
# build.py's docstring, which has the measurement).
build/

# Vivado's PS7 board-preset automation writes a summary into a directory named
# from an unset variable, next to wherever it was launched.  Noise, not output.
NA/

# JLCPCB API responses: 5 MB, re-fetched on demand, and every entry is stamped
# with the time of its own query so it goes stale by design.  The pricing that
# matters is already baked into mfg/release/annotated_bom.md.
mfg/jlc_cache.json

# Pre-rewrite snapshots of the placer sources.  The three that existed were
# byte-identical to commit b40dae4, so they were deleted rather than tracked;
# `git show b40dae4:GPSDO-PYNQ-Z2/pcb/<file>.py` is the recovery.  The rule
# stays as insurance in case something makes more of them.
*.r14

# gateware/ has its own .gitignore for the Vivado project and build tree.
